From: Marc Herrero <marcht@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: only disconnect the route a mixer control owns

Each AudioReach virtual mixer route control ("<BE> Audio Mixer <FE>")
connects the FE stream graph to the BE device graph by storing the source
module in the device graph's audioreach_graph_info. A write of 0 to any of
these controls clears that link unconditionally, even when the device
graph is connected to a different FE.

With two front ends that can feed the same back end this makes the result
depend on write order. On QCS6490 (Radxa Dragon Q6A):

  - alsactl restore writes 'DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0 Audio Mixer MultiMedia2' = 1
    and then 'DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0 Audio Mixer MultiMedia1' = 0, which leaves
    DisplayPort disconnected although the saved state has it connected;
  - the UCM HDMI enable sequence writes
    'RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0 Audio Mixer MultiMedia2' = 0, which disconnects
    MultiMedia1 from the headphones. A PCM started on MultiMedia1 then never
    advances (hw_ptr stays 0).

Only drop the link when it belongs to the control being cleared, i.e. when
audioreach_is_vmixer_connected() is true for it. A write of 0 to a control
that is not the active route is now a no-op, matching what its get()
already reports.

Signed-off-by: Marc Herrero <marcht@proton.me>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c	2026-11-11 09:06:25.400413255 +0000
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/topology.c	2026-11-11 09:06:25.409275652 +0000
@@ -1176,7 +1176,7 @@
 	if (ucontrol->value.integer.value[0]) {
 		audioreach_connect_sub_graphs(data, scontrol, dapm_scontrol, true);
 		snd_soc_dapm_mixer_update_power(dapm, kcontrol, 1, NULL);
-	} else {
+	} else if (audioreach_is_vmixer_connected(data, scontrol, dapm_scontrol)) {
 		audioreach_connect_sub_graphs(data, scontrol, dapm_scontrol, false);
 		snd_soc_dapm_mixer_update_power(dapm, kcontrol, 0, NULL);
 	}
